Define the shared workbench visual system: system UI typography, monospaced code, neutral surfaces, consistent borders/spacing and terracotta emphasis. Style the fixed tool rail, expression/output panes, object list and tabbed inspector. Give live controls generous space, position designer preview between outline and properties, and adapt to narrow screens without document overflow.


Style the discovery actions, contextual inspector help, examples search, observed-result card and persistent view result with responsive wrapping.

Emphasize the returned value over its actions: large scalar text, plain multiline text, explicit object inspection and a secondary identity. Keep long outputs scrollable within their result. Put secondary actions in a compact expandable area. Sidebar object tools use ordinary navigation styling rather than implying a currently selected tool.

Place a compact starter selector in the expression heading. Collection previews show indexed rows with wrapping contents and bounded scrolling.
